{"obsah":"<p>We were riding on several fronts practically all weekend. On Saturday Martin Šimůnek and Míra Brunclík did the traditional Forestry Day near Česká Lípa. Michal Budský and Tobík Dolák, meanwhile, went wild on the folding obstacle set at a children's day in Český Jiřetín. And the biggest workload fell to Vlasta, Lukáš Valný and Nikolka Kabeláčová at one stop of the L'Etape amateur road races, followed by a transfer to the summer welcome in Doudleby nad Orlicí.</p>\n\n<p>At first L'Etape was an intimate event, and our job was to entertain the spectators until the main part of the programme and the riders arrived. Of course we also entertained the organising team, whom we thank for the cooperation and hospitality. We had limited time, and after the exhibition only a few minutes to clear the area and flee ahead of the main peloton. Doudleby, by contrast, was a bigger event with a few hundred spectators, where we had a space next to the main stage and ran both an exhibition with volunteers – where the main star was the local history teacher – and a tape-jump contest, which ended in a draw between a local football star and Vlasta in a great atmosphere.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FDSC_0683.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FDSC_0683.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250848\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FDSC_0680-rotated.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FD